{
  "uid": "infrastructure",
  "title": "Infrastructure",
  "description": "The machine and the containers on it. Request rates, ticks and alerts live on the Crypto Alerts dashboard; this one answers why a container restarted.",
  "tags": [
    "crypto-alerts",
    "infrastructure"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "container",
        "label": "Container",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(container_memory_rss{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}, name)",
        "query": "label_values(container_memory_rss{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}, name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {},
        "options": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Containers",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Peak memory against its limit",
      "description": "The highest anonymous memory each container reached in the last hour, against its ceiling. Three deliberate choices. Anonymous rather than total, because page cache is reclaimed on demand and a healthy container reads 99% of its limit by total usage. Peak rather than current, because a Go service saws between collections — Grafana swings from 132 MiB to 450 MiB inside a 640 MiB limit, so a single reading is a number picked at random from that range while the peak is what the OOM killer sees. And an instant query, which makes the hour-long window cost about 1700 samples instead of the 1.7M a range query would.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 75
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "expr": "100 * max_over_time(container_memory_rss{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[1h]) / (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory breakdown — $container",
      "description": "The panel ticket 09 needed and did not have. `docker stats` adds these three together and reports the sum, which is how a flat process looked like a leaking one: the growth was the kernel's reclaimable dentry cache, charged to the cgroup but belonging to no process. Anonymous is what a kill is decided on; page cache and slab are reclaimed first.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "limit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.stacking",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "none"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_rss{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "anonymous"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_cache{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "page cache"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_kernel_usage{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "kernel / slab"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=\"$container\"} > 0",
          "legendFormat": "limit"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Uptime",
      "description": "Seconds since each container last started, on a logarithmic axis so a container up for four minutes and one up for nine days are both readable. A restart is a fall to the bottom, and it stays visible wherever it happened rather than ageing out of a window. This is the automation of what ticket 09 did by hand: comparing start times in `docker inspect` to work out which container had quietly died.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "log",
              "log": 10
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "time() - container_start_time_seconds{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Healthcheck state",
      "description": "What each container's own probe currently reports. Containers without a healthcheck report -1 and are filtered out. This is the piece that turns a restart into a story: a probe that had been failing for minutes before the restart says something different from one that was healthy right up to the kill.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "healthy",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "unhealthy",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "expr": "container_health_state{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} != -1",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU",
      "description": "Cores consumed per container, and where a ceiling exists, the ceiling. The host has two vCPUs, so the sum of these against 2 is the honest measure of how much room is left. Only the telemetry services are capped; the application services are deliberately uncapped.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisLabel": "cores"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_spec_cpu_quota{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} / container_spec_cpu_period{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}} limit"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Reclaim forced at the ceiling",
      "description": "cgroup v2's memory.events \"max\" counter: how many times the kernel had to reclaim because a container hit its limit. Nothing dies, so this is invisible in restarts and in `docker inspect` — and it is exactly what the API container was doing 160 times in two days while its `docker stats` figure sat at 96.7% of the limit. A container that is quietly reclaiming at its boundary is fine right up until the moment it is not.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "increase(container_memory_events_max_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[10m]) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory pressure (PSI)",
      "description": "The fraction of wall-clock time in which every task in the container was stalled waiting for memory. This is the kernel's own verdict on whether a container is struggling, and it does not require inferring anything from percentages: zero means comfortable, anything sustained above it means the container is spending its life waiting for pages.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_memory_stalled_seconds_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[5m]) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "OOM kills",
      "description": "Two independent witnesses, plotted as raw counters rather than as increase() over a window. A kill is rare, and a counter that steps from zero to one goes on saying so forever, while a rate over a window says it for ten minutes and then forgets — the wrong memory for the one event you look up after the fact. cAdvisor names the container; the kernel's own counter, by way of node-exporter, says it happened at all. Both were previously readable only through journalctl -k behind sudo.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_oom_events_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "node_vmstat_oom_kill",
          "legendFormat": "host, since boot"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
